    "created_at": "2021-10-20T08:58:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-20T08:58:27Z",
    "body": "This is unfortunately an issue with how Terminal.app handles character width - an issue either addressed or configurable by most other terminal emulators.\r\nI'd recommend either looking into the open-source iTerm2 or configuring Starship to add extra padding before the symbol, like so:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# ~/.config/starship.toml\r\n\r\n[nodejs]\r\nsymbol = \"  \"\r\n#           ^ Your browser may not show the NerdFonts symbol in the line above, but it's there\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
